cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Separating Intrinsic Variability from Structural Inconsistency in Pairwise Comparisons: Identification and a Scalable Mixture-of-Preferences Estimator"
message: "If you use this code, please cite the paper."
repository-code: "https://github.com/lihaoahu/mop"
url: "https://github.com/lihaoahu/mop"
abstract: "Estimates, from pairwise comparisons, how many preference states a population occupies, what each one ranks, and how inconsistently each is executed. Intrinsic variability enters through the mixture, structural inconsistency through a component-specific dispersion; the dispersion is identified only where the variance function leaves it free."
keywords:
  - preference learning
  - pairwise comparisons
  - mixture model
  - Bayesian inference
